  annotation "note_1771591707892_1", anchor: "opening his jaws for witnesses who had, by that point, drowned, scattered, or stopped listening", text: "Rend Kzulrora taught that strength means nothing without the pack's witness. Krathund learned the lesson perfectly and then outlived every witness who could validate it. The collection makes sense once you see it this way — artifacts cannot observe, but they can be held, arranged, retrieved. They are a replacement congregation. He was not hoarding power. He was hoarding presence. Things that would stay when pods would not. That he refused the name *the-collector* only confirms it; he knew what the collection meant and could not bear the accuracy.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771591707892_2", anchor: "pressing the Shroud's volcanic glass pages against the dead flesh of his flank where he could not feel them burning", text: "My earlier annotation on the Shroud noted it kills anyone who attempts duplication. Whether pressing it against nerve-dead flesh constitutes a workaround or simply meant he died slightly slower than he would have otherwise — the accounts do not distinguish strategy from indifference, and by this point in the narrative, I am not sure Krathund did either.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
